'' TWO MODULES, EACH WITH A PRIVATE nextId HOLDING A CONSTRUCTED STATIC, LINK. The static's
'' one-time guard is named after its storage -- NEXTID$c$init in both -- and went out
'' external where the storage is internal, so this pair failed with 'lld-link: duplicate
'' symbol: NEXTID$c$init'. fbc emits nothing external for it (llvm-nm, measured 2026-09-27).
''
'' THE PROGRAM IS RUN: 11 then 12, which is fbc's output on win64 and Linux alike. The
'' second static starts at 10 too -- module two declares Cnt's constructor, module one
'' defines it -- and each module's static is its own object, counted by its own guard.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target win64-msvc tests/driver/src/static-guard-a.bas tests/driver/src/static-guard-b.bas -o tests/driver/staticguard.exe
'' ENV: TKO_LIBPATH=toolchains/tiko-windows/lib/win64-msvc
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: duplicate symbol
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/driver/staticguard.exe
'' RUN: tests/driver/staticguard.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 11
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: 12
